# Snapshot superset ≠ Ridge freeze

Full note: `docs/research/010-snapshot-superset-vs-ridge.md`. Do not reopen `docs/roadmap/04-bcw-v0.1.md`.

- **Store** leakage-safe FPI/SP+-class families on snapshots. Ridge v0.1 stays small and explainable; freeze its `feature_version` on **2009–2022** only.
- **Before Ridge freeze:** HFA, Elo, **SRS**, **opponent-adjusted EPA**, logistic, then Ridge. Compare Ridge(raw EPA) vs Ridge(adj EPA) in that window. Spec: `docs/research/011-model-lab-reproductions.md`.
- SRS is a baseline **model**, not an ensemble. Opp-adj EPA is a lab model and a candidate Ridge family — still PURE, still `known_at < kickoff`, prior opponent strength only.
- After freeze: LightGBM, NGBoost, \(F_M\), FPI-style Power Index (ST/QB/travel), classifier shootout, consensus. Not v0.1.
- Do not add ESPN FPI, close/`vegas_wp`, injuries, weather, news, or LightGBM to anything labeled PURE before freeze.
- Recency: last-3/5 and EWMA α grid on **2009–2022**; do not stuff all correlated versions into Ridge.
